course: dictionary
lesson: 3887
title: Words for people from a place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A Frenchman is a man who comes from France or is French. The ending -man shows it is about a man. A woman from France is a Frenchwoman.
explain: The context helps here. «Napoleon was about average height for a Frenchman of his time» is a sentence about height, so a Frenchman is a man from France. Try it: put "a man from France" in place of "a Frenchman" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Be careful with a stereotype. «A Frenchman in a striped shirt and beret» is a joke picture from cartoons, not the truth. One man from France is one person, and he cannot stand for everyone from France.
fact: A Frenchman is a man who comes from France or is French.
fact: A Frenchwoman is a woman who comes from France or is French.
fact: «Descartes, a Frenchman of the 1600s, tried doubting everything» shows that a Frenchman can be a famous thinker.
fact: Louis Braille was a Frenchman who invented a way for blind people to read by touch.
fact: In old history books, «Frenchman» can also mean a French person or soldier in general, but this use is informal.
exercise: «Napoleon was about average height for a Frenchman of his time.» What is a Frenchman? | *A man from France | A kind of bread | A woman from France | A cartoon in a striped shirt
exercise: Which word is the name for a woman from France? | A beret | The French | Frenchman | *Frenchwoman
exercise: Is «a Frenchman in a striped shirt and beret» the truth about every French man? | Yes, it is a true picture of France | *No, it is a joke from cartoons, not the truth | Yes, every Frenchman wears a beret
test: Descartes, «a Frenchman of the 1600s», tried doubting everything. What is a Frenchman? | A woman who sells bread | *A man from France | A soldier from Spain
test: Louis Braille was a Frenchman. What country does he come from? | Germany | Spain | Italy | *France
exam: «Napoleon was about 1.69 metres tall, an ordinary height for a Frenchman of his time.» Here, a Frenchman means | A cartoon picture | *A man from France, living in his time | A soldier only | A woman from France
